## Why This Is Asked
Realistic multi-tenant feature flags require low latency, strict tenant isolation, and cross-region resilience to meet production demands.

## Key Concepts
- AWS AppConfig tenant-scoped configurations
- Per-tenant IAM boundaries and policy enforcement
- Low-latency delivery via edge caching or streaming mechanisms
- Cross-region disaster recovery with automated failover
- Comprehensive auditing through CloudTrail integration

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code: fetch flag for tenant with caching
async function fetchFlag(tenantId, flagName) {
  // Retrieve from AppConfig with tenant scoping
  const config = await appconfig.getConfiguration(
    `tenant-${tenantId}`, 
    flagName
  );

  // Cache in DynamoDB for sub-millisecond access
  await dynamodb.put({
    TableName: 'feature-flags',
    Item: {
      tenantId,
      flagName,
      value: config.value,
      ttl: Date.now() + 30000 // 30s TTL
    }
  });

  return config.value;
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

This validates practical isolation in a shared data lake, ensuring least privilege and scalable onboarding. It also tests policy layering and auditing capabilities.

## Key Concepts

- IAM roles per tenant with strict resource boundaries
- Trust policies tied to the tenant app identity
- S3 prefix-scoped permissions with bucket or IAM policy conditions
- Onboarding automation for new tenants and centralized governance
- Cross-tenant test plans and auditing hooks

## Code Example

```json
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": ["s3:ListBucket"],
      "Resource": "arn:aws:s3:::corp-data-lake",
      "Condition": {"StringLike": {"s3:prefix": "tenant-<tid>/*"}}
    },
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": ["s3:GetObject","s3:PutObject"],
      "Resource": "arn:aws:s3:::corp-data-lake/tenant-<tid>/*",
      "Condition": {"StringEquals": {"aws:PrincipalTag/tenant-id": "<tid>"}}
    }
  ]
}
```

```json
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
